 that provides online counselling and therapy services through websites, mobile applications, phones, and text-based interactions by its licensed clinicians. The company offers its products and services under the Teladoc and BetterHelp brands. It serves employers, health plans, hospitals and health systems, insurance companies, and financial services companies, as well as individual members. The company was formerly known as Teladoc, Inc. and changed its name to Teladoc Health, Inc. in August 2018. Teladoc Health, Inc. was incorporated in 2002 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Charles  Divita III, CPA | CEO & Director | Age 55 | Compensation: $1.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 4K people. Revenue per employee of $544K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, improving at 42%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $61K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $17K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Teladoc Health, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.6B market cap on $2.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years and +42% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory. Operating margins are expanding by +6.2pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -56% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 73% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $285M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 11 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -17.3% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -13.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-6.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (17.7% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins 11% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 43% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.4297297297297298},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 58/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 58% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Teladoc Health (TDOC) Shares Just Climbed, So What Is Driving Attention Now?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/healthcare/nyse-tdoc/teladoc-health/news/teladoc-health-tdoc-shares-just-climbed-so-what-is-driving-a","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793850277.165,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.421,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"TDOC Q3 deep dive: insurance-fueled BetterHelp pivot offsets cash pay headwinds, new care model launches","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/tdoc-q3-deep-dive-insurance-035736513.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793678256.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.843,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","product"]},{"title":"Teladoc Health (NYSE:TDOC) Stock Price Target Raised at Oppenheimer","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/02/teladoc-health-nysetdoc-stock-price-target-raised-at-oppenheimer.html","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793639236.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Teladoc Health (NYSE:TDOC) Stock Dropped to \u201cSell\u201d by Argus","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/02/teladoc-health-nysetdoc-stock-dropped-to-sell-by-argus.html","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793628414.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.7,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Teladoc Health, Inc. (NYSE:TDOC) Released Earnings